# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
# "What affects the cost" section for each service page, rendered after the main body, and the
# "Questions to ask before you hire" checklist used on the service + city pages.
# No prices are stated here: real pricing depends on the client's rates and each site visit.
# (The instant electrical estimate uses the client's own prices from site.config.json.)

COSTS = {
"panel-upgrades": """<p>Panel upgrade prices depend mostly on whether the service size changes. Swapping a panel at the same size costs less than a 100 to 200 amp upgrade, which adds a new meter base, mast and service cable. Underground services, moving the panel, the number of circuits to reconnect, grounding updates and any utility charges all affect the total. Fuse boxes and very old panels often need more circuit work to reconnect safely.</p>""",
"ev-charger-installation": """<p>EV charger installation costs depend on the distance from the panel to where you park, the charger's amperage, whether the run is indoors, outdoors or buried to a detached garage, and whether your panel has the capacity and space. An energy management system or panel upgrade adds to the price when the panel is too small. Supplying the charger is extra if you haven't bought one.</p>""",
"generator-installation": """<p>Generator hookup prices depend on the setup: an inlet and panel interlock is the simplest, a transfer switch with selected circuits costs more, and a standby generator hookup costs the most. The distance from the panel to the generator, the number of circuits, a dedicated sump pump circuit and the gas connection (by a gas fitter) all affect the total.</p>""",
"surge-protection": """<p>Whole-home surge protector prices depend on the device's rating, whether your panel has a free space or needs a breaker rearranged, and the condition of the grounding. Installing one during other panel work, such as an upgrade or an EV charger, usually costs less than a separate visit.</p>""",
"home-rewiring": """<p>Rewiring costs depend on the size of the house, how much is being replaced, access through attics and basements, plaster or drywall walls, and how many outlets, switches and fixtures are on each circuit. Aluminum connection repairs cost less than replacing circuits. Patching, a panel upgrade and any knob and tube removal are priced as part of the scope.</p>""",
"knob-and-tube-replacement": """<p>Knob and tube replacement is priced by how much is still live, how many floors it serves, access from the attic and basement, plaster walls and the number of outlets and fixtures on each run. Insulation in the attic, a panel upgrade and patching affect the total. An assessment first means the quote reflects the actual house.</p>""",
"pot-lights": """<p>Pot light prices depend on the number of lights, what's above the ceiling (an attic, another floor or open joists), the ceiling material, how many switches and dimmers, and the fixtures chosen. Colour-selectable or premium fixtures, plaster ceilings, high ceilings and patching affect the total.</p>""",
"outlets-switches": """<p>Outlet and switch work is priced by the number of devices, whether new wire must reach them from the panel or a nearby circuit, wall type (drywall, plaster, brick or tile), and whether dedicated circuits are needed. GFCI, USB, smart and specialty devices cost more than standard outlets and switches.</p>""",
"renovation-wiring": """<p>Renovation electrical is priced by the number of circuits, outlets, switches and lights, the appliances being connected, whether the walls are open or closed, and whether the panel needs more capacity. Kitchens with induction ranges, basements with bedrooms and bathrooms, and additions or garages with subpanels cost more than simpler room updates.</p>""",
"hot-tub-wiring": """<p>Hot tub and pool wiring costs depend on the tub's amperage, the distance from the panel, whether the wire runs along the house or is buried, the panel's capacity and space, and the bonding needed. Pool pumps, heaters, lights and extra outdoor outlets add to the total.</p>""",
"electrical-repair": """<p>Repair costs depend on how long it takes to find the cause, what needs replacing and where it is. Some fixes are a single device; others are damaged cable inside a finished wall or a failing panel component. We tell you the cause and the cost of the fix before we do it.</p>""",
"emergency-electrician": """<p>Emergency call costs depend on the time of day, what's needed to make the system safe, and the repair itself. Making it safe comes first; the permanent repair is often quoted separately once the cause is clear. Damage to the service or meter base can also involve the utility.</p>""",
"electrical-inspections": """<p>Inspection prices depend on the size and age of the house, the number of panels and outbuildings, and whether you want photos and repair costs in the report. Inspecting a single concern, such as a panel or one circuit, costs less than a whole-house inspection.</p>""",
"commercial-electrical": """<p>Commercial work is priced by scope: the size of the space, the number of circuits, fixtures and equipment connections, three-phase requirements, after-hours scheduling and coordination with other trades. LED retrofits are priced per fixture, with lifts or special access added where needed.</p>""",
}

